From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] odhcpd: exclude the header from Reconfigure option length

The DHCPv6 authentication option length describes its payload, excluding
the four-byte option header. Subtract that header from the packed structure
size so authenticated Reconfigure messages carry a valid option boundary.
No lease or retransmission lifetime is changed.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/src/dhcpv6-ia.c
+++ b/src/dhcpv6-ia.c
@@ -194,7 +194,7 @@ static int send_reconf(struct dhcpv6_lea
 	};
 	struct dhcpv6_auth_reconfigure auth = {
 		.type = htons(DHCPV6_OPT_AUTH),
-		.len = htons(sizeof(struct dhcpv6_auth_reconfigure)),
+		.len = htons(sizeof(struct dhcpv6_auth_reconfigure) - DHCPV6_OPT_HDR_SIZE),
 		.protocol = 3,
 		.algorithm = 1,
 		.rdm = 0,
